'''Emmanuel''' "'''Manny'''" '''Arceneaux''' (born September 17, 1987) is an American former professional [[gridiron football|football]] [[wide receiver]] who  played 11 seasons in the [[Canadian Football League]] (CFL) for the [[BC Lions]], [[Saskatchewan Roughriders]], and [[Edmonton Elks]]. He played [[college football]] for the [[Alcorn State Braves football|Alcorn State Braves]].

Arceneaux signed as an [[undrafted free agent]] with the Lions in 2009. He was also a member of the [[Minnesota Vikings]], [[Washington Redskins]], [[New York Jets]], and [[Frisco Fighters]].
